# Commercial S12.1 r1 timer clock-domain preflight diagnosis

The fresh read-only server preflight found the S11 controller timer enabled,
active and waiting with a finite next run, but systemd exposed that run through
`NextElapseUSecMonotonic`. The r1 controller required only
`NextElapseUSecRealtime`, which is empty for the reviewed activation-relative
`OnActiveSec` / `OnUnitActiveSec` timer. The r1 deployment therefore remained
unattempted and no runtime, repository, systemd, nginx or evidence mutation
occurred.

The minimal r2 correction accepts a finite next elapse in either systemd clock
domain while retaining all enabled/active/waiting requirements. Empty, `n/a`,
zero and infinite values remain fail-closed. Focused tests cover realtime,
monotonic, absent and non-finite postures. The immutable r1 freeze is not moved
or reused.
